{
  "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
  "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner Narkis Golan, a United States citizen, married respondent Isacco Saada, an Italian citizen, in Italy, where they had a son, B. A. S., in 2016. In 2018, Golan few with B. A. S. to the United States to attend a wedding and, instead of returning to Italy, moved into a domestic violence shelter with B. A. S. Saada thereafter timely fled a petition with the U. S. District Court for the Eastern District of New York, seeking an order returning B. A. S. to Italy pursuant to the Hague Convention."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Saada",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Saada's primary argument is that determining whether a grave risk of harm exists necessarily requires considering whether any ameliorative measures are available."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court granted Saada's petition after a 9-day bench trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court directed the parties to appear for status conferences and to submit status reports and supplemental briefs, and the court corresponded with the U. S. Department of State and the Italian Ministry of Justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Italian court overseeing the underlying custody dispute issued a protective order barring Saada from approaching Golan for one year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Italian court ordered that an Italian social services agency oversee Saada's parenting classes and therapy and that visits between Saada and B. A. S. be supervised."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court additionally ordered Saada to pay Golan $150,000 to facilitate B. A. S.' return to Italy and to cover Golan's and B. A. S.' living costs while they resettled."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Saada",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Saada's primary argument is that this requirement is implicit in the Convention's command that the court make a determination as to whether a grave risk of harm exists."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Saada",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Saada argues that the approach of other signatory countries, including the United Kingdom, supports the position that consideration of ameliorative measures is required."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0014",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, for example, it took the District Court nine months to comply with the Second Circuit's directive on remand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1034",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b686ce3baeceade91a82826fc80957c3ba46062679b3d0eba88b20fd25a2f84",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b686ce3baec-0001-0013",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The judgment of the United States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit is vacated, and the case is remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
